{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.EinsteinAnomalyOperator\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.AlgebraicStationarity\n\nPurely algebraic stationarity layer for doubled-carrier operator dynamics.\n\nThis file introduces no external time, coordinates, or variational calculus.\nStationarity is expressed only through vanishing expectations of Lie/commutator\nderivations. The core surfaces are:\n\n- stationarity of an observable along a given transport generator,\n- global algebraic stationarity under all inner generators,\n- the modular curvature operator as the `K = Jε` nested commutator,\n- and the gauge/source balance equivalent to state-level algebraic stationarity.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.AlgebraicStationarity\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovTransport\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.StateDependentTransport\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.ConformalUnification\nopen InfoGeometry.Krein\n\nsection Core\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\nlocal notation \"Kop\" => InfoGeometry.Canonical.TomitaTakesaki.modularComplexI (E := E)\n\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedRing EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedAlgebra ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsTopologicalRing EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : CompleteSpace EndH := inferInstance\n\n/--\nA state is stationary along the transport generator `X` when the expectation of\nthe corresponding inner derivation of `A` vanishes.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ndef IsStationaryAlong\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) : Prop :=\n  ω (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A) = 0\n\n/--\nAn observable is algebraically stationary when every inner derivation has zero\nexpectation in the state `ω`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ndef IsAlgebraicallyStationary\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH) : Prop :=\n  ∀ X : EndH, IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω X A\n\n/--\nState-indexed algebraic stationarity for the modular dynamics generated by a\nstate-dependent datum.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ndef IsStateAlgebraicallyStationary\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E) (ψ : H₂) (A : EndH) : Prop :=\n  ω (stateInducedDynamics (E := E) M ψ A) = 0\n\n/--\nGauge/source cancellation law for a state-induced modular derivation.\n\nThis is the algebraic balance form of the transport equation: the expectation of\nthe gauge branch is exactly the negative of the source branch.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ndef AlgebraicEinsteinBalance\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E) (ψ : H₂) (A : EndH) : Prop :=\n  ω (stateGaugeDynamics (E := E) M ψ A)\n    =\n  -ω (stateSourceDynamics (E := E) M ψ A)\n\n/-- The modular curvature operator is the doubled `K = Jε` commutator of `D`. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def modularCurvatureOperator\n    (D : EndH) : EndH :=\n  operatorInformationHessian (E := E) Kop D\n\n@[rep_depth transport, simp] theorem isStationaryAlong_iff\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) :\n    IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω X A\n      ↔\n    ω (observableLieDerivation (E := E) X A) = 0 := by\n  simp [IsStationaryAlong]\n\n@[rep_depth transport, simp] theorem isAlgebraicallyStationary_iff\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH) :\n    IsAlgebraicallyStationary (E := E) ω A\n      ↔\n    ∀ X : EndH, ω (observableLieDerivation (E := E) X A) = 0 := by\n  simp [IsAlgebraicallyStationary, IsStationaryAlong]\n\n/--\nState algebraic stationarity is exactly stationarity along the derived modular\ngenerator at the chosen state.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem isStateAlgebraicallyStationary_iff_generatorStationarity\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E) (ψ : H₂) (A : EndH) :\n    IsStateAlgebraicallyStationary (E := E) ω M ψ A\n      ↔\n    IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω (stateRelativeModularGenerator (E := E) M ψ) A := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\nState algebraic stationarity is equivalent to exact gauge/source cancellation in\nexpectation.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem isStateAlgebraicallyStationary_iff_algebraicEinsteinBalance\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E) (ψ : H₂) (A : EndH) :\n    IsStateAlgebraicallyStationary (E := E) ω M ψ A\n      ↔\n    AlgebraicEinsteinBalance (E := E) ω M ψ A := by\n  constructor\n  · intro hStat\n    unfold IsStateAlgebraicallyStationary AlgebraicEinsteinBalance at *\n    rw [stateInducedDynamics_eq_gauge_add_source (E := E) M ψ A] at hStat\n    exact add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg.mp (by simpa using hStat)\n  · intro hBalance\n    unfold IsStateAlgebraicallyStationary AlgebraicEinsteinBalance at *\n    rw [stateInducedDynamics_eq_gauge_add_source (E := E) M ψ A]\n    exact by\n      simpa using (add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg.mpr hBalance)\n\n/--\nProjector-agreement closure turns Einstein-anomaly stationarity into\nprojector-obstruction stationarity on the same observable.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem starCertifiedEinsteinAnomalyStationary_iff_projectorObstructionStationary_of_projectorAgreement\n    (SCI : StarCertifiedConformalInference E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH)\n    (hEq :\n      SCI.liftedEinsteinAnomalyOperator\n        =\n      -SCI.toCertifiedConformalInference.liftedProjectorObstructionOperator) :\n    IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω SCI.liftedEinsteinAnomalyOperator A\n      ↔\n    IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω\n      SCI.toCertifiedConformalInference.liftedProjectorObstructionOperator A := by\n  constructor\n  · intro hStat\n    unfold IsStationaryAlong at hStat ⊢\n    rw [hEq] at hStat\n    have hPos := congrArg Neg.neg hStat\n    simpa [operatorInformationFirstVariation, transportCommutator, sub_eq_add_neg, add_comm] using hPos\n  · intro hStat\n    unfold IsStationaryAlong at hStat ⊢\n    rw [hEq]\n    have hNeg := congrArg Neg.neg hStat\n    simpa [operatorInformationFirstVariation, transportCommutator, sub_eq_add_neg, add_comm] using hNeg\n\nend Core\n\nsection LightweightTheorems\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\nlocal notation \"Kop\" => InfoGeometry.Canonical.TomitaTakesaki.modularComplexI (E := E)\n\n/-- Negating the generator negates the induced commutator variation. -/\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem operatorInformationFirstVariation_neg_left\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) (-X) A\n      =\n    -operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A := by\n  unfold operatorInformationFirstVariation transportCommutator\n  simp\n  abel\n\n/-- Negating the observable negates the induced commutator variation. -/\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem operatorInformationFirstVariation_neg_right\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X (-A)\n      =\n    -operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A := by\n  unfold operatorInformationFirstVariation transportCommutator\n  simp\n  abel\n\n/-- The zero observable is algebraically stationary in every state. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem isAlgebraicallyStationary_zero\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) :\n    IsAlgebraicallyStationary (E := E) ω (0 : EndH) := by\n  intro X\n  unfold IsStationaryAlong operatorInformationFirstVariation transportCommutator\n  simp\n\n/-- Commutation with a fixed generator implies stationarity along that generator. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem isStationaryAlong_of_commute\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH)\n    (hComm : Commute X A) :\n    IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω X A := by\n  have hZero : operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A = 0 := by\n    unfold operatorInformationFirstVariation transportCommutator\n    exact sub_eq_zero.mpr hComm.eq\n  unfold IsStationaryAlong\n  rw [hZero]\n  simp\n\n/-- Central observables are algebraically stationary in every state. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem isAlgebraicallyStationary_of_central\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH)\n    (hCentral : ∀ X : EndH, Commute X A) :\n    IsAlgebraicallyStationary (E := E) ω A := by\n  intro X\n  exact isStationaryAlong_of_commute (E := E) ω X A (hCentral X)\n\n/-- The phase-axis response is the negative `K`-variation of the observable. -/\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem phaseAxisResponse_eq_neg_KVariation\n    [CompleteSpace E]\n    (D : EndH) :\n    phaseAxisResponse (E := E) D\n      =\n    -operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) Kop D := by\n  simp [phaseAxisResponse, phaseAxisForce, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n    transportCommutator,\n    InfoGeometry.Canonical.TomitaTakesaki.modularComplexI_eq_complex_i (E := E)]\n\n/--\nApplying the `K`-derivation to the phase-axis response produces minus the\nmodular curvature operator.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem KVariation_phaseAxisResponse_eq_neg_modularCurvature\n    [CompleteSpace E]\n    (D : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) Kop (phaseAxisResponse (E := E) D)\n      =\n    -modularCurvatureOperator (E := E) D := by\n  unfold phaseAxisResponse phaseAxisForce modularCurvatureOperator\n  unfold operatorInformationHessian operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation\n  unfold operatorInformationFirstVariation transportCommutator\n  simp [InfoGeometry.Canonical.TomitaTakesaki.modularComplexI_eq_complex_i (E := E)]\n  abel\n\n/--\nIf the phase response of `D` is stationary under the internal phase axis `K`,\nthen the expectation of the modular curvature operator vanishes.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem modularCurvatureExpectation_eq_zero_of_phaseResponseStationary\n    [CompleteSpace E]\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (D : EndH)\n    (hStat : IsStationaryAlong (E := E) ω Kop (phaseAxisResponse (E := E) D)) :\n    ω (modularCurvatureOperator (E := E) D) = 0 := by\n  unfold IsStationaryAlong at hStat\n  rw [KVariation_phaseAxisResponse_eq_neg_modularCurvature (E := E) D] at hStat\n  simpa using hStat\n\nend LightweightTheorems\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.AlgebraicStationarity\n","mtime":1777928003332}